\pard\ltrpar\pard\ltrpar\s1\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\outlinelevel9\sb0\sa0\sbauto0\saauto0\nowidctlpar\sl0\hyphpar1\rtlch\af10\afs24\alang1033\ltrch\dbch\af10\afs24\alang1033\hich\af10\afs24\alang1033\loch\f10\fs24\cf0\nosupersub\charscalex100
\expndtw0\b0\scaps0\ulnone\ulc0\striked0\i0\kerning1\strike0\v0\caps0\lang1033\chcbpat0\highlight0 I want to build a free and open source Manufacturing Execution System (MES) that will be designed, coded and tested solely
 by an AI (you).  The code should never need to be looked at or maintained by a human, but rather by an AI coding agent.  Therefore the implementation should be optimized for ease of maintenance and enhancements by an AI,
 not by a human.\par
\par
The duration of the project will be many weeks and will cross sessions, therefore there must be a procedure in place to resume work where a previous session left off without needing to understand the implementation from s
cratch.  Also, I need to be able to refer to a module of functionality by an identifier for enhancements rather than describe what it does to save time and token expense.\par
\par
The project deliverable will be an MES framework with plug-in functionality (much like a coding IDE has plugins).  An end user will download the framework from GitHub and proceed to customize the functionality based on th
eir unique requirements.  Using their preferred IDE (e.g. Claude Code, Visual Studio Code, etc.) , they will describe to the AI agent what customizations they require, and the AI will proceed to implement them.\par
\par
The first task is to create and document a project plan describing step-by-step what implementation tasks will be accomplished.  I will decide if a task has been completed and we will move on to the next task.\par
\par
\pard\ltrpar\pard\ltrpar\s2\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\outlinelevel0\sb240\sa60\sbauto0\saauto0\nowidctlpar\sl0\keepn\hyphpar1\keep\rtlch\af10\afs36\alang1033\ab\ltrch\dbch\af9\afs36\alang1033\ab\hich\af10\afs36\alang1033\ab\loch\f10\fs36
\cf0\nosupersub\charscalex100\expndtw0\b1\scaps0\ulnone\ulc0\striked0\i0\kerning1\strike0\v0\caps0\lang1033\chcbpat0\highlight0 Features\par
\pard\ltrpar\pard\ltrpar\s1\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\outlinelevel9\sb0\sa0\sbauto0\saauto0\nowidctlpar\sl0\hyphpar1\rtlch\af10\afs24\alang1033\ltrch\dbch\af10\afs24\alang1033\hich\af10\afs24\alang1033\loch\f10\fs24\cf0\nosupersub\charscalex100
\expndtw0\b0\scaps0\ulnone\ulc0\striked0\i0\kerning1\strike0\v0\caps0\lang1033\chcbpat0\highlight0 A MES is software used in a factory to produce goods effectively.  It interfaces to an Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) 
at inbound touchpoints (e.g. production orders, and manufactured materials) as well as at outbound touchpoints (e.g. work in process reporting and consumption of raw materials).  An MES also interfaces to production equip
ment controllers (e.g. Programmable Logic Controllers or PLCs and microcontrollers) as well as test equipment for test results.\par
\par
An MES tracks the progress of work-in-process (WIP)  represented by units or lots of material through the physical model of production lines, work centers and equipment.  A dispatching algorithm upon the occurance of a pr
oduction event decides what work center or equipment to move the work (unit or lot) to.  The dispatching could be manual in which case an operator enters a disposition mapped to a destination.  Or the dispatching could be
 automated based on the downstream equipment\u8217\'92s capability and capacity to  receive additional work.\par
\par
The end user will use an IDE such as Claude Code or VS Code to implement new features.  We will use VS Code to develop the MES framework.  A Git repository will be used to store all artifacts from which the end user will 
download the framework and proceed to make their customizations.\par
